Description of problem:

[https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/assisted_installer_for_openshift_container_platform/2025/html/installing_openshift_container_platform_with_the_assisted_installer/customizing-with-bundles-and-operators#lvm-storage-operator_customizing-with-bundles-and-operators]
{code:none}
One of the LVMS requirements in this list states "Requires 1 additional CPU core for each non-boot drive." which is excessive. LVMS does not require any additional CPU cores for each drive. It just requests "cpu=5, mem=50Mi for the operator (== per installation), and cpu=5m, mem=45Mi per Node".  {code}
Slack thread for further context:

[https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C060V75JF4J/p1766407149179929]

